.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH exec 1  "exec " 
.SH NAME
exec \- Run a command with strict agent\-safe defaults (clears the inherited environment, strips MURK_KEY, requires \-\-only, masks injected values in the output)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmurk agent exec\fR [\fB\-\-allow\-operator\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-reserved\fR] [\fB\-\-vault\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-only\fR> <\fICOMMAND\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a command with strict agent\-safe defaults (clears the inherited environment, strips MURK_KEY, requires \-\-only, masks injected values in the output)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-only\fR \fI<ONLY>\fR
Inject these specific keys (required — agent mode fails closed)
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-operator\-key\fR
Decrypt with a key that is not an agent grant: your own stored key from ~/.config/murk/keys, or a full recipient\*(Aqs MURK_KEY or MURK_KEY_FILE. Without this, agent exec needs an agent grant key
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-reserved\fR
Allow keys named like loader/shell/tool variables (PATH, LD_*, GIT_*, MURK_*, ...)
.TP
\fB\-\-vault\fR \fI<VAULT>\fR [default: .murk]
Vault filename
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fICOMMAND\fR>
Command and arguments to execute
